## **3. SW1 — Cisco Catalyst 3560**

### **3.1 Basic configuration**

```
enable
configure terminal

hostname SW1
no ip domain-lookup
enable secret <ENABLE_SECRET>
```

### **3.2 Create VLANs**

```
vlan 10
 name SALE
 exit

vlan 20
 name SUPPORT
 exit

vlan 99
 name Management
 exit

vlan 101
 name Lab_R1
 exit

vlan 102
 name Lab_R2
 exit
```

| VLAN | Name       | Purpose           |
| ---- | ---------- | ----------------- |
| 1    | Default    | Default VLAN      |
| 10   | SALE       | Lab segmentation  |
| 20   | SUPPORT    | Lab segmentation  |
| 99   | Management | Device management |
| 101  | Lab_R1     | R1 lab network    |
| 102  | Lab_R2     | R2 lab network    |

### **3.3 Configure management SVI**

SVI stands for Switched Virtual Interface.

```
interface Vlan99
 ip address <SW1_MGMT_IP> 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
 exit
```

### **3.4 Configure access ports**

AT&T gateway-facing port:

```
interface FastEthernet0/<PORT>
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 99
 no shutdown
 exit
```

R1-facing port:

```
interface FastEthernet0/<PORT>
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 99
 no shutdown
 exit
```

R2-facing port:

```
interface FastEthernet0/<PORT>
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 99
 no shutdown
 exit
```

### **3.5 Configure Layer 2 default gateway**

```
no ip routing
ip default-gateway <ATT_GATEWAY_IP>
```

The original baseline used AT&T as the management gateway. We changed the switch gateway to R2 during the later VPN implementation, which is intentionally excluded here.

