# **Part II — SSH remote management**

## **6. Configure SSH on SW1, R1 and R2**

The following configuration applies individually to all three devices.

### **6.1 Configure domain name**

```
configure terminal
ip domain-name homelab.local
```

### **6.2 Create local administrator**

```
username <ADMIN_USERNAME> privilege 15 secret <ADMIN_PASSWORD>
enable secret <ENABLE_SECRET>
```

### **6.3 Generate RSA keys**

```
crypto key generate rsa
```

When prompted, select a supported modulus size, preferably 2048 bits.

Alternatively, on supported IOS versions:

```
crypto key generate rsa modulus 2048
```

### **6.4 Enable SSH version 2**

```
ip ssh version 2
ip ssh time-out 60
ip ssh authentication-retries 3
```

### **6.5 Configure VTY lines**

```
line vty 0 4
 login local
 transport input ssh
 exec-timeout 15 0
 exit
```

For devices supporting additional VTY lines:

```
line vty 5 15
 login local
 transport input ssh
 exec-timeout 15 0
 exit
```

### **6.6 Disable unnecessary web management**

```
no ip http server
no ip http secure-server
```

### **6.7 Save configuration**

```
end
write memory
```

Or:

```
copy running-config startup-config
```

## **7. Verify SSH server configuration**

