## **10. Troubleshoot legacy SSH algorithms**

Our older Cisco IOS devices did not support some of the modern algorithms enabled by default in Windows OpenSSH.

### **10.1 Enable verbose debugging**

```
ssh -v <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

```
ssh -vv <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

```
ssh -vvv <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

### **10.2 Resolve key exchange mismatch**

```
ssh -oKexAlgorithms=+diffie-hellman-group1-sha1 <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

### **10.3 Resolve host key mismatch**

```
ssh -oHostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-rsa <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

### **10.4 Resolve encryption cipher mismatch**

```
ssh -oCiphers=+aes128-cbc <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

### **10.5 Resolve MAC algorithm mismatch**

```
ssh -oMACs=+hmac-sha1 <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

### **10.6 Final working SSH command**

This is the combined legacy compatibility command we used.

```
ssh -oKexAlgorithms=+diffie-hellman-group1-sha1 -oHostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-rsa -oCiphers=+aes128-cbc -oMACs=+hmac-sha1 <USERNAME>@<DEVICE_IP>
```

| Parameter         | Purpose                        |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |
| KexAlgorithms     | Key exchange negotiation       |
| HostKeyAlgorithms | Server identity verification   |
| Ciphers           | Session encryption             |
| MACs              | Message integrity verification |

These are legacy cryptographic algorithms. Restrict their use to the isolated lab rather than enabling them globally or exposing SSH directly to the internet.

## **11. Simplify SSH using Windows SSH config**

Instead of typing the entire command every time, configure individual SSH host aliases.

### **11.1 Create or open SSH configuration file**

```
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force "$HOME\.ssh"
notepad "$HOME\.ssh\config"
```

### **11.2 Configure aliases**

```
Host SW1
    HostName <SW1_MGMT_IP>
    User <SW1_USERNAME>
    KexAlgorithms +diffie-hellman-group1-sha1
    HostKeyAlgorithms +ssh-rsa
    Ciphers +aes128-cbc
    MACs +hmac-sha1

Host R1
    HostName <R1_MGMT_IP>
    User <R1_USERNAME>
    KexAlgorithms +diffie-hellman-group1-sha1
    HostKeyAlgorithms +ssh-rsa
    Ciphers +aes128-cbc
    MACs +hmac-sha1

Host R2
    HostName <R2_MGMT_IP>
    User <R2_USERNAME>
    KexAlgorithms +diffie-hellman-group1-sha1
    HostKeyAlgorithms +ssh-rsa
    Ciphers +aes128-cbc
    MACs +hmac-sha1
```

### **11.3 Connect using aliases**

```
ssh SW1
ssh R1
ssh R2
```

# **Part IV — Troubleshooting and corrections**

## **12. Management SVI not operational**

### **Inspect interface status**

```
show ip interface brief
show interfaces Vlan99
show vlan brief
show interfaces status
```

On routers:

```
show vlan-switch brief
```

### **Correct VLAN assignment**

```
configure terminal
interface <MANAGEMENT_PHYSICAL_PORT>
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 99
 no shutdown
 exit

interface Vlan99
 no shutdown
 exit
```

The management VLAN generally needs at least one active Layer 2 port in a forwarding state for its SVI to become operational.

## **13. Incorrect default routing**

### **On R1 and R2**

```
show ip route
show running-config | include ip route
```

Remove an incorrect default route:

```
configure terminal
no ip route 0.0.0.0 0.0.0.0 <OLD_GATEWAY>
```

Configure the correct default route:

```
ip route 0.0.0.0 0.0.0.0 <CORRECT_GATEWAY>
```

### **On SW1**

```
show running-config | include ip default-gateway
show running-config | include ip routing
```

```
configure terminal
no ip routing
no ip default-gateway <OLD_GATEWAY>
ip default-gateway <CORRECT_GATEWAY>
```

## **14. SSH version mismatch**

```
show ip ssh
```

```
